s\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [39, 490, 1373, 1598], \"page_id\": 79}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 56, 103, 79], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"66\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [465, 128, 1033, 153], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"FEDERAL AGENCIES' FINANCIAL REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 297, 726, 558], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"Section 114 of the Budget and Accounting Procedures Act of 1950 (31 U.S.C. 3513a) requires the Secretary of the Treasury to prepare reports on the financial operations of the U.S. Government and provides that each executive agency must furnish the Secretary of the Treasury such reports and information relating to the agency's financial condition and operations as the Secretary may require. The provisions do not apply to the legislative and judicial branches of the Federal Government; however, these entities are encouraged to submit the prescribed reports so the Secretary of the Treasury can prepare comprehensive reports on all the financial activities of the U.S. Government.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 585, 724, 898], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"The Treasury Financial Manual (1 TFM 2-4100) sets the criteria for the submission of annual and quarterly financial reports in accordance with the Reporting Entities Listing (Bulletin No. 88-11). Reports are provided for six fund types: Revolving funds, trust revolving funds, 15 major trust funds, all other trust funds, all other activity combined, and consolidated reports of an organizational unit. The financial transactions supporting the required reports are to be accounted for on the accrual basis. The Report on Operations can be submitted on a cash basis under certain circumstances (see 1 TFM 2-4180.20). Reports are to be prepared from a budgeting and accounting system which contains an integrated data base that is part of the agency's integrated financial management system as required by the Office of Management and Budget (OMB) Circular No. A-127.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 918, 723, 1042], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"The required reports should include all assets, liabilities, and equities relating to all programs and activities under control of the reporting entity, except for the assets of disbursing officers, which are reported by the Treasury. Reports should include transfer appropriation accounts from other agencies, foreign currencies, opera-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [653, 207, 845, 230], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [772, 297, 1425, 369], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"tions conducted in the territories or overseas, and any monetary assets or property received, spent, or otherwise accounted for by the reporting entity. Amounts are reported to the dollar.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [772, 396, 1425, 729], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"Requirements provide that Federal agencies submit to Treasury four financial reports supplemented by three supporting reports. These reports are: Report on Financial Position (SF 220), Report on Operations (SF 221), Report on Cash Flow (SF 222), and Report on Reconciliation (SF 223). The three supporting reports are: Direct and Guaranteed Loans Reported by Agency and Program Due from the Public (SF 220-8), Report on Accounts and Loans Receivable Due from the Public (SF 220-9), and Additional Financial Information (SF 220-1). The report on Direct and Guaranteed Loans is submitted to Treasury quarterly, and annually for publication in the Treasury Bulletin. The Report on Accounts and Loans Receivable Due from the Public is submitted quarterly on a selected basis, and by all entities annually. Information captured in the SF 220-8 is shown in the following table:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [772, 778, 1169, 801], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"Table FA-1.--Direct and Guaranteed Loans\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [772, 824, 1423, 992], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"This report reflects the direct loans and guaranteed loans to the public through the Federal Credit Program to support credit activities. Actual control of credit program levels remains with authorizing legislation and appropriations acts. The report on Direct and Guaranteed Loans also provides the Federal Reserve Board information to monitor the flow of funds. An accompanying chart depicts direct loans and guaranteed loans for the second quarter of fiscal 1990.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1395, 59, 1444, 95], \"page_id\": 81}], \"content\": \"67\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [480, 111, 1063, 144], \"page_id\": 81}], \"content\": \"FEDERAL AGENCIES' FINANCIAL REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [383, 169, 1155, 199], \"page_id\": 81}], \"content\": \"Table FA-1.\\u2014Direct and Guaranteed Loans, March 31, 1990\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [437, 201, 1086, 230], \"page_id\": 81}], \"content\": \"(In thousands of dollars. Source: SF 220-8; compiled by Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [80, 232, 1434, 1665], \"page_id\": 81}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Agency and prog