s $30,220 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [61, 65, 88, 83], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"76\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [472, 126, 1011, 151], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"INTERNATIONAL FINANCIAL STATISTICS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [61, 209, 716, 310], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"These indices are presented to provide measures of the general foreign exchange value of the dollar that are broader than those provided by single exchange rate levels. They do not purport to represent a guide to measuring the impact of exchange rate levels\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [760, 209, 1420, 310], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"on U.S. international transactions. The indices are computed as geometric averages of individual currency levels with weights derived from the share of each country's trade with the United States during 1982-83.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [260, 400, 1223, 432], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"Table IFS-4.--Trade-Weighted Index of Foreign Currency Value of the Dollar\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [477, 441, 972, 461], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"Source: Office of Foreign Exchange Operations--International Affairs\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [54, 466, 1410, 1226], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Date</th><th>Index of industrial country currencies 1</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">Annual average (1980 = 100) 2</td></tr><tr><td>1980</td><td>100.0</td></tr><tr><td>1981</td><td>109.1</td></tr><tr><td>1982</td><td>119.7</td></tr><tr><td>1983</td><td>125.2</td></tr><tr><td>1984</td><td>133.5</td></tr><tr><td>1985