24,881,621</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [87, 1216, 358, 1241], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"See footnotes at end of table ESF-2.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [544, 1261, 994, 1295], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"Table ESF-2.--Income and Expense\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [667, 1302, 843, 1325], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"(In thousands of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [87, 1327, 1449, 1726], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>Current quarter<br>Jan. 1, 1990,<br>through<br>Mar. 31, 1990</th><th>Year to date<br>Oct. 1, 1989,<br>through<br>Mar. 31, 1990</th></tr><tr><td><b>Income and expense:</b></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Profit (loss) on:<br>Foreign exchange</td><td>(722,204)</td><td>(395,451)</td></tr><tr><td>Adjustment for change in valuation of SDR holdings and allocations 1.</td><td>(40,177)</td><td>53,006</td></tr><tr><td>Interest (net charges) on:<br>Special drawing rights</td><td>82,960</td><td>157,910</td></tr><tr><td>U.S. Government securities</td><td>15,411</td><td>33,419</td></tr><tr><td>Foreign exchange</td><td>222,322</td><td>420,547</td></tr><tr><td><b>Income from operations</b></td><td>(441,688)</td><td>269,431</td></tr><tr><td><b>Net income</b></td><td>(441,688)</td><td>269,431</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [85, 1751, 752, 1878], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"1 Beginning July 1974, the International Monetary Fund (IMF) adopted a technique for valuing the special drawing rights (SDRs) based on a weighted average of exchange rates for the currencies of selected member countries. The U.S. SDR holdings and allocations are valued on this basis beginning July 1974.\\n2 Excludes foreign exchange transactions for future and spot delivery.\\n3 A non-interest-bearing liability to the U.S. Treasury resulting from the transfer to the Exchange Stabilization Fund of foreign currencies drawn from the IMF by the United States.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [785, 1753, 1447, 1844], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"Note.-Annual balance sheets for fiscal years 1934 through 1940 appear in the 1940 Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury and those for succeeding years appear in subsequent reports through 1980. Quarterly balance sheets beginning with Dec. 31, 1938, have been published in the Treasury Bulletin. Data from inception to Sept. 30, 1978, may be found on the statements published in the January 1979 Treasury Bulletin.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [440, 181, 964, 763], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [508, 779, 889, 812], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"SPECIAL REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [421, 1708, 1403, 1873], \"page_id\": 127}], \"content\": \"CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS OF THE UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT FISCAL YEAR 1989/PROTOTYPE\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [49, 52, 98, 76], \"page_id\": 128}], \"content\": \"114\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [595, 155, 850, 182], \"page_id\": 128}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 268, 1301, 374], \"page_id\": 128}], \"content\": \"The fiscal year 1989 edition of the Consolidated Financial Statements of the United States Government was recently released. The statements and accompanying information, prepared and published annually by Treasury's Financial Management Service, are unique since they are developed on the accrual basis of accounting and modeled after corporate-type reports.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 398, 1306, 619], \"page_id\": 128}], \"content\": \"This general purpose report provides, for instance, a snapshot of what the Federal Government owns and owes in presenting summary information on its financial condition and operations. Data originate in program agency accounting systems Governmentwide and are captured in the five consolidated statements of: Financial position, operations, changes in financial position, receipts and outlays, and reconciliation of accrual operating results to the cash basis budget. The customary notes to financial statements and several broad supplemental tables, ranging from accounts and loans receivable due from the public to Federal obligations, complete the publication's content.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [146, 646, 1305, 752], \"page_id\": 128}], \"content\": \"An extract of the 1989 statements is published in this issue of the Treasury Bulletin. The excerpts will give readers a view of some of the most noteworthy information in the statements. The entire 40-page document is for sale through the Superintendent of Documents, U.S. Government Printing Office. An order form is printed at the end of the Bulletin.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1387, 59, 1429, 86], \"page_id\": 129}], \"content\": \"115\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [79, 162, 1065, 208], \"page_id\": 129}], \"content\": \"CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [82, 253, 803, 316], \"page_id\": 129}], \"content\": \"United States Government Consolidated Statement of Financial Position as of September 30, 1989 and 1988\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [79, 323, 1400, 1137], \"page_id\": 129}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>($ billions)</th><th>1989</th><th>1988</th></tr><tr><td>Total assets</td><td>1,210.0</td><td>1,176.4</td></tr><tr><td>Total liabilities</td><td>3,777.3</td><td>3,586.2</td></tr><tr><td>Accumulated position</td><td>-2,567.3</td><td>-2,409.8</td></tr></table><table><tr><th>United States Government Consolidated Statement of Operations for the Years Ended September 30, 1989 and 1988 ($ billions)</th><th>1989</th><th>1988</th></tr><tr><td>Total revenues</td><td>1,087.8</td><td>1,039.2</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>1,237.3</td><td>1,171.8</td></tr><tr><td>Excess of expenses over revenues</td><td>-149.5</td><td>-132.6</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [465, 1219, 1038, 1846], \"page_id\": 129}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [58, 61, 100, 88], \"page_id\": 130}], \"content\": \"116\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [53, 164, 640, 212], \"page_id\": 130}], \"content\": \"FINANCIAL HIGHLIGHTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [54, 279, 492, 320], \"page_id\": 130}], \"content\": \"Revenues and expenses\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [53, 358, 1389, 490], \"page_id\": 130}], \"content\": \"The following graphs show revenues and expenses for fiscal years 1987 through 1989, and the major categories of revenues by source and expenses by agency for fiscal 1989. Certain revenue amounts have been reported on the accrual basis and differ from those reported on the cash basis. The data supporting the graph of expenses by agency are also reported on the accrual basis and differ from those reported on the cash basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [341, 598, 1130, 688], \"page_id\": 130}], \"content\": \"TOTAL REVENUES AND TOTAL EXPENSES FISCAL YEARS 1987-89\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [183, 706, 1221, 1444], \"page_id\": 130}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1396, 61, 1439, 81], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"117\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [92, 158, 539, 203], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"Revenues and expenses\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [264, 417, 726, 454], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"MAJOR SOURCES OF REVENUES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [598, 262, 953, 314], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"FISCAL YEAR 1989\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [97, 494, 775, 973], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [920, 1065, 1439, 1124], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"MAJOR CATEGORIES OF EXPENSES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [777, 1133, 1086, 1216], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"Health and Human Services\\nSocial Security Administration\\n17%\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1088, 1133, 1447, 1573], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1350, 1408, 1423, 1516], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"Other 19%\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 1289, 991, 1368], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"d Human Servic