ar II\", this suggests there might be a significant dip during that period.\n\nI realize I need the exact number of local maxima in each plot to answer the question. The data spans different economic periods, and each plot likely reflects the economic fluctuations of its time. Without precise visual data, I'm working with general observations about economic trends during these years.\n\nI'll investigate the underlying data to get more precise information about the plot's characteristics.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_dd2a227afb1b401a9a6b6976","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1990_09.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\n# Let's find if there's any numerical data stored in the JSON\n# that might represent the chart data\nfor elem in data['document']['elements']:\n    content = elem.get('content', '')\n    if content and 'GDP' in content.upper():\n        bbox = elem.get('bbox', [{}])[0]\n        print(f\\\"Page {bbox.get('page_id')}: {content}\\\")\n\" | head -30"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
